package main

// The `Int -> Go.Any` want seeds only the lambda body's result —
// an unannotated lambda parameter is a fresh meta that the body's
// own uses bind first (lambda params have no annotation form —
// docs/problems/2026-11-01-lambda-param-forms.md). `a == x` binds
// `a` to `Int` from the use site, so the residual unify of
// `Int -> Bool` against `Go.Any -> Bool` reports the honest
// mismatch. The binding must name the parameter's type through a
// `let`/`fn` signature on the surrounding declaration instead.
fn g (x: Int) -> Go.Any -> Bool = fn a -> a == x
fn main () -> Unit = ()
